<title>ITALY: Italy's Naples sees Sept CPI at 3.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Naples sees Sept CPI at 3.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>NAPLES 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Naples said its September consumer price index stood at 0.4 percent month-on-month and 3.3 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In August, Naples' inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 3.4 percent respectively.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.64 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to August 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.4   (0.1)     3.3  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.5   (0.2)     4.5  (4.8)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0   (0.0)     1.8  (1.9)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.2   (0.7)     0.8  (7.6)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.1   (0.1)     2.0  (2.0)</p>
<p>    Health services		  -0.3   (0.0)     1.2  (1.9)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.2   (0.1)     8.7  (8.8)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     1.7   (0.1)     3.7  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.2   (0.0)     0.9  (0.2)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.1)     3.7  (4.4)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.6   (0.1)     2.5  (2.0)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom ++392 66129526</p>
